    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Will Smith** stands out as our premier option with a 65.28 efficiency score. Leading off against Landen Roupp, **Will Smith** benefits from a high-leverage lineup spot and a favorable xERA of 4.07, maximizing his run-scoring potential. **Masyn Winn** also presents a strong profile at 60.24, bolstered by a 10% park factor bump that helps mitigate the challenge of facing a lefty. While **Brendan Donovan** is hitting leadoff against Burrows, his 59.45 score sits just on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier; his value is heavily propped up by a 14% platoon advantage, making him a high-floor play despite a neutral park environment.\n\nWe are forced to navigate significant headwinds against Sheehan, who carries a stingy 3.16 xERA. This matchup suppresses the outlook for **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee**. **Luis Arraez** remains a staple in our lineup at 46.01, though his upside is clearly capped by the SP skill penalty. The most difficult bench decision was **Drew Gilbert**, who hovered at 36.01. While **Drew Gilbert** projects well, the combination of a low-value #8 batting order spot and the difficulty of facing Sheehan pushed him below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" Similarly, **Wenceel Perez** failed to crack the starting nine (34.70) due to a poor platoon matchup and a defensive penalty against an elite catcher, forcing us to prioritize lineup stability over his raw skill.\n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding the pending lineups for **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee**. Because all three are locked into a matchup against Sheehan, any unexpected movement toward the bottom of the batting order could further erode their efficiency. We are effectively punting offensive explosion in those slots to preserve our daily caps, banking on the stability of **Will Smith** and **Masyn Winn** to carry the load. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Geraldo Perdomo** currently inactive, our depth is thin; we must rely on these mid-tier projections to sustain our 5x5 standing until the rest of our roster, including **Cal Raleigh**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Bryson Stott**, return to higher-probability environments.",
